CREA v2  —  n8n Hands Layer
2.0.0 · 2026-09-09

Standalone, client-owned automation pack: a WhatsApp AI booking assistant
plus the shoot-ops automations (Acuity intake, confirmations, chase, card
pipeline, invoicing, morning briefing, listing leads).

What v2 is
- Runs entirely under the buyer's own accounts. No shared services, ids,
  paths or labels — the conversation state store and alert sink are folded
  into vault-api/server.js, and the pack ships its own error workflow
  (crea-00-error-handler).
- CREA_VAULT_DIR points storage at your Obsidian vault so Obsidian Sync
  backs up every booking, lead and invoice. See DATA-AND-BACKUP.md.
- One command: ./go-live.sh. Handover to someone else: HANDOVER.md.

Verified 2026-09-09 end to end on n8n 2.30.7 against a live model:
answered from the knowledge file ($450 quoted verbatim, nothing invented),
checked availability without confirming a slot, captured the shoot brief
across turns, handed the owner a quote-ready enquiry, wrote the lead note;
consecutive messages route correctly; LLM-down falls through to the
deterministic 5-question qualifier; Acuity intake, card-pipeline human
gate and the error handler all reach their designed end.
